 "text": "Basketball started with two peach baskets. Springfield, Massachusetts. It's winter. Too cold to play outside. A young gym teacher, James Naismith, gets a challenge from his boss. Invent an indoor game to keep his students active. Fun fact, Naismith wasn't even American. He was Canadian. He grabs a soccer ball. He nails two peach baskets ten feet up. He writes 13 rules. Then the class plays the very first game. December 21st. Nine players aside. And the final score? One to nothing. Plus, in those early games, every time someone scored, a janitor had to climb a ladder to get the ball back. Those 13 rules became one of the most popular sports on Earth. Every legend has a beginning.",
